# Held-out answer key. Authored from each paper's TITLE AND ABSTRACT ONLY, with
# no retrieval run against any question until this file was committed. That is
# the whole point: the development key in retrieval.jsonl was written alongside
# the system, so a question that retrieved badly could be reworded until it did
# not, and its numbers cannot rule that out. These were frozen first and scored
# once, and whatever they scored is what is reported.
#
# Papers were chosen before any question existed, by a fixed rule: current
# papers with 25-90 body passages, excluding every paper already named in the
# development key and every subject probed by hand while building the system,
# grouped by primary category, every 37th taken, then every 6th of those.
#
# Shapes: mostly plain subject questions. Four are deliberately phrased as
# comparisons ("differ", "versus", "compare") with a SINGLE answering paper -
# the case the development key has none of, and the one needed to price what
# the comparison-gated title leg costs when the question only looks compound.
#
# No definitional or covered-but-unanswered cases: deciding that a subject is
# covered while the question goes unanswered requires inspecting the corpus,
# which is exactly what authoring blind forbids. Those live in the development
# key, where that inspection is honest.
